From 9e5093720e9da45670d98ca4e0f7d903cd503b8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:29:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] refactor(chat): provider attempts, the non-stream retry
 and the sandbox step leave stream_chat
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fourth step of the split.

- provider_stream.ProviderAttempt: one `acompletion(stream=True)` call —
  start, iterate chunks while merging usage, close upstream on
  disconnect, `finish()` merges the wrapper's final usage and estimates
  tokens when the provider sent none, `usage_event()` builds the ledger
  event. `estimate_tokens()` replaces three copies of the tokenizer
  fallback. `NonStreamRetry` is the one-shot `stream=False` retry after a
  dropped stream body, with its own `chat_completion_retry` events.
- code_interpreter_turn: `CodeInterpreterLoop` bookkeeping,
  `run_sandbox_until_stopped` (Stop-aware wait, drained abandon) and
  `describe_code_step` (result formatting, artifact storage, the feedback
  message the model continues from).
- stream_chat's loop now reads: start attempt -> forward chunks -> absorb
  the attempt -> decide (empty / nudge / sandbox / continue); the three
  exception handlers book the in-flight attempt through the same
  `_absorb` helper instead of three copies of `capture_usage_event(...)`.
  `_persist_content` and `_review_agent_output` fold four repeated blocks.

The provider function and the sandbox runner are injected from
proxy_service's module globals, so tests keep patching
`proxy_service.acompletion` / `run_python_sandbox`.

stream_chat: 1194 -> 521 lines, cyclomatic complexity ~150 -> 75;
proxy_service 2777 -> 1370 lines. Not yet at the plan's <300 / <25 —
the remaining bulk is the chunk loop with its interleaved yields; next
step is a TurnRunner class (see APPLY.md). 1371 tests, contract and
cancellation tests unchanged; mypy baseline shrinks to 181.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
